<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net48</TargetFramework>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <BaseOutputPath>.\bin</BaseOutputPath>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    A test project of its own, and the separation is the point.

    TiaMcpServer.Test starts a TIA Portal in [AssemblyInitialize], because almost everything it
    covers needs one. That cost lands on every test in that assembly whether it needs a portal or
    not, so the governance tests took twelve seconds and could not run at all on a machine without
    TIA Portal installed.

    CLAUDE.md requires the opposite of the governance layer: those tests must run without TIA
    Portal, because a safety rule that can only be checked on a licensed machine is a safety rule
    that stops being checked. That is only true if they live outside that assembly — hence this
    project.

    Nothing here may take a dependency that needs TIA Portal at run time, and since 2026-09-02
    nothing here may take one that needs it at *build* time either. The reference below is to
    TiaMcpServer.Portable, which references no Siemens package at all — not to TiaMcpServer, which
    references the Openness resolver and therefore cannot be compiled on a machine without a
    licence. That one line is what puts these tests on a hosted CI runner; pointing it back at
    TiaMcpServer would take them off it again without breaking anything locally, which is exactly
    how it would happen.

    No inherited debt: this project is new, and a real finding here gets fixed rather than
    suppressed. CA1307 was the first, and it was fixed by using the StringComparison overload.

    The two entries below are not debt. They are repository-wide style decisions already taken and
    justified in src/TiaMcpServer/TiaMcpServer.csproj, and repeating the decision is better than
    having the same code style pass in one project and fail in another.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);IDE0008</NoWarn>  <!-- var: CLAUDE.md asks for judgement the analyzer cannot make -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CA1861</NoWarn>   <!-- constant arrays as arguments: a hot-path concern, in test setup -->
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="17.14.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="MSTest" Version="3.9.2" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\TiaMcpServer.Portable\TiaMcpServer.Portable.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Using Include="Microsoft.VisualStudio.TestTools.UnitTesting" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
